                  <zone fixed-size='829' forceUpdate='true' h='98000' id='18' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='17750' x='81583' y='1000'>
                    <formatted-text>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>KEY INSIGHTS: </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>- Liquidity Buffer Trend &amp; CFP Threshold — Key Insights</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>+ Liquidity Deterioration:</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'> The liquidity buffer declined during the stress period, reflecting the cumulative impact of reduced cash inflows and increased cash outflows.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>+ CFP Trigger:</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'> The pre-funding liquidity buffer fell below the 3,500 billion VND threshold on 13–14 March 2023, triggering the Contingency Funding Plan (CFP).</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>+ Liquidity Stabilization:</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'> Following funding injections totaling 477.11 billion VND, the post-funding buffer recovered to the 3,500 billion VND threshold on the trigger dates.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>+ Recovery Trend:</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'> The buffer subsequently recovered, indicating an improvement in liquidity under the model assumptions. Continued monitoring remains necessary to assess whether the recovery is sustainable.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>- CFP Triggered on 13/03–14/03</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>Liquidity buffer before funding fell below the 3,500 billion VND threshold on two days.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>- Funding Utilization</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>Total funding drawn: 477.11 billion VND, including 346.32 billion on 13/03 and 130.80 billion on 14/03.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>-  </run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>Remaining Funding Capacity</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>1,022.89 billion VND remained available at the end of the monitoring period.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>- Minimum Liquidity Buffer</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='12'>The lowest buffer before funding was 3,153.68 billion VND on 13/03.</run>
                    </formatted-text>
